quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  19,12,"(We later said:) ‘O Yahya (John)! Hold on to the Book (i.e. the Torah) firmly. And We granted him wisdom (and prophethood) while he was still a child,"
  19,13,and (We granted him) compassion and purity from Our presence; and he was God-conscious.
  19,14,"And he was kind to his parents, and he was neither arrogant nor disobedient."
  19,15,"Peace be upon him, the day he was born, the day he dies, and the day he will be raised alive!"
  19,16,And mention Maryam (Mary) in the Book when she withdrew from her family to an eastern place.
  19,17,"So, she secluded herself from them. Then We sent Our Spirit (the Angel Gabriel) to her, who appeared before her as a perfect human."
  19,18,She said: ‘I seek refuge from you in the Most-Compassionate (Lord) if you are conscious (of Allah).’
  19,19,He (Gabriel) said: ‘I am only a messenger from your Lord so that I may bestow upon you a pure son.’
  19,20,"She said: ‘How shall I have a son when no man has ever touched me, nor have I been unchaste?’"
  19,21,He (Gabriel) said: ‘So shall it be. Your Lord says: ‘It is easy for Me. And so that We may make him a sign for humankind and a mercy from Us. And it is a matter (already) decided.’
  19,22,"So, she conceived him, then withdrew with him to a distant place."
  19,23,"And the pains of childbirth drove her to the trunk of a palm tree. She said: ‘Oh, I wish I had died before this and become a thing completely forgotten from memory!’"
  19,24,"Then he called her from below her (saying): ‘Do not worry. Surely, your Lord has made a spring to flow beneath you."
  19,25,Shake towards you the trunk of the palm tree; it will deliver fresh ripe dates to you.
